# Run with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client):
# click "Send Request" above a request, or press Ctrl+Alt+R.
#
# These call the fake Oura API from e2e/fakeoura, not the server and never
# the real Oura. Start the end-to-end environment and keep it up first:
#
#   KEEP_E2E_UP=1 scripts/e2e-test.sh
#
# The client ID and secret are the made-up ones e2e/compose.yaml gives the
# fake. Send the requests in order: later ones use the tokens that "issue"
# and "refresh" return.

@fakeOuraUrl = http://localhost:8081
@clientId = e2e-client
@clientSecret = e2e-client-secret

### Health check
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/health

### Reset: forget every token, document and pending failure
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/_control/reset

### Seed sleep data, served exactly as given
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/_control/seed
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "daily_sleep": [{ "day": "2026-11-01", "score": 82 }],
  "sleep": [{ "day": "2026-11-01", "type": "long_sleep", "average_hrv": 42, "lowest_heart_rate": 51 }]
}

### Issue a token pair, as completing the Oura login would
# @name issue
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/_control/tokens

### Daily sleep for a day range, with the access token
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/v2/usercollection/daily_sleep?start_date=2026-11-01&end_date=2026-11-01
Authorization: Bearer {{issue.response.body.access_token}}

### Sleep periods for a day range, with the access token
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/v2/usercollection/sleep?start_date=2026-11-01&end_date=2026-11-01
Authorization: Bearer {{issue.response.body.access_token}}

### Without an access token: 401
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/v2/usercollection/sleep?start_date=2026-11-01&end_date=2026-11-01

### Refresh: a new token pair for the issued refresh token
# @name refresh
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{issue.response.body.refresh_token}}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### The same refresh token again: 400 invalid_grant, because each works once
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/oauth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token={{issue.response.body.refresh_token}}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### Make the next sleep request fail with 503
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/_control/failures
Content-Type: application/json

{ "endpoint": "/v2/usercollection/sleep", "status": 503, "count": 1 }

### Sleep with the refreshed access token: 503 once, then 200 when sent again
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/v2/usercollection/sleep?start_date=2026-11-01&end_date=2026-11-01
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.access_token}}

### Expire every access token issued so far
POST {{fakeOuraUrl}}/_control/expire-access-tokens

### Sleep with the now expired access token: 401
GET {{fakeOuraUrl}}/v2/usercollection/sleep?start_date=2026-11-01&end_date=2026-11-01
Authorization: Bearer {{refresh.response.body.access_token}}
